      "text": "\\begin{align*} n &\\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}, \\\\ n &\\equiv 2 \\pmod{5}.\\end{align*}Let $n = 4x+3$. We substitute into the expression above, and we get that\n$4x+3\\equiv 2 \\pmod{5}$. Applying bash, (adding $3$), we get that\n$4x \\equiv -1 \\pmod{5}$. Multiplying both sides by $4$, we get that\n$16x \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5} \\implies x \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5}$. Therefore, $x = 5k+4$ for $k \\ge -1$. Substituting this value of $x$ into our first equation, we get that $n = 4(5k+4) + 3 = \\boxed{20k+19}$. The answer is 20k+19",
